\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slips vs yen, hurt by BoJ's absence.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 15:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comment; changes byline, dateline, previous LONDON)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 18 (Reuters) - The dollar retreated on Thursday, undermined by the yen's broad rally amid a surge in Japanese equity inflows and the Bank of Japan's seeming absence from the marketplace, analyst said.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials have warned they would act against sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves but speculation \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is scaling back its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to suppress the appreciating yen against the dollar helped the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise for the fourth consecutive day.  \par \par \uc2 Positive U.S. economic data caused a brief, moderate rise in the dollar against the euro, as markets focused on the yen's price movement across the board.  \par \par \uc2 The Producer Price Index, which measures prices paid to farms and refineries, climbed to a steeper-than-expected 0.6 percent in January after a 0.2 percent gain in December. Markets were expecting a 0.4 percent rise.  \par \par \uc2 "The PPI numbers suggest there may be more inflation ...than previously expected," said Michael Woolfolk, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New York.  \par \par \uc2 "This is expected to filter through to CPI and will definitely be on the Fed's radar. This may mean that the Fed can begin removing its accommodative stance sooner than expected. This is positive for the dollar because it will remove the interest rate differential," he added.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. initial jobless claims fell to 336,000 in the week ended March 13, well below the market's forecast of 345,000. While this is the lowest level in more than three years, analysts wondered when the improvement in this data is going to be reflected in the non-farm payrolls report.  \par \par \uc2 In morning New York trade, the dollar fell to a one-month low of 106.62 yen , before trading back up to 106.90, down over 1 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The euro also fell sharply against the yen, dropping to a six-week trough of 130.82 yen , but traded back up to 131.49 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the euro rose to $1.2294 , benefiting from the greenback's losses versus the yen, though the euro remained stuck in the broad range it has adopted since hitting a record high at $1.2927 in mid-February. Sterling was trading firmer at $1.8263 .  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN, ECB, SWISS POLICIES  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei stock average hit its highest in nearly two years and data showed overseas investors continued their buying spree of Japanese stocks last week, while Japanese investors stepped up repatriation of their overseas investments last week ahead of their March 31 book-closings.  \par \par \uc2 "Everybody is speculating whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and looking at the movement in dollar/yen since Monday you would think so - or at least it hasn't been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week," said Niels Christensen, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale.  \par \par \uc2 "With the strong performance of the Nikkei, Japanese and foreign investors are moving more funds back to Japan."  \par \par \uc2 Also, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB), in its regular twice-monthly council meeting in Frankfurt on Thursday, made no statement on interest rates. Analysts said this was not surprising since monetary policy was not expected to be on the agenda.  \par \par \uc2 The Swiss National Bank left interest rates unchanged on Thursday, saying it did not wish to threaten Switzerland's economic upswing by raising rates too soon. The decision had no impact on the market, analysts said, with the dollar trading lower at 1.2690 francs .  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Burton Frierson in London).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040318e03i002a7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
