\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen flexes muscles vs dollar, euro as BOJ absent.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson  \par \uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 12:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 18 (Reuters) - The yen rose to one-month highs against the dollar and six-week peaks on the euro on Thursday as foreigners bought Tokyo stocks, locals brought home overseas investments and the Bank of Japan remained conspicuously absent.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials warned they would act against sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves but speculation \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was scaling back its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to suppress the yen against the dollar helped the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise for the fourth day in a row.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei stock average hit its highest in nearly two years and government data showed overseas investors continued their buying spree of Japanese stocks last week, while Japanese investors stepped up repatriation of their overseas investments last week ahead of their March 31 book-closings.  \par \par \uc2 "The capital flows into Japan remain strong. We had the flow data overnight, which showed strong continued evidence of inflows into Japan," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez.  \par \par \uc2 "We know that the speculative market has become short yen. On top of that the pullout of the Japanese authorities continues to be played on by the market. The market now is buying the yen on the back of all of these factors."  \par \par \uc2 By the late European morning, the yen had risen more than 1.35 percent from its previous New York close to 106.62 per dollar, its strongest since February 19.  \p