s suspected foreigners' stock buying was driving the rally.  \par \par \uc2 According to government data released on Thursday, overseas investors continued their buying spree of Japanese stocks last week, purchasing 129.6 billion yen ($1.20 billion) worth.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  OVER?  \par \par \uc2 Speculation was growing that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is rethinking its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy because of concerns about exposure to domestic interest rate rises, which would drive up funding costs, and worries about losses on ballooning holdings of U.S. Treasury securities.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "simply out of habit", while top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi reiterated on Thursday that Tokyo had not changed its stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the authorities might be waiting for the unwinding of long positions in the dollar that had built up after it recently shot up to 112 yen.  \par \par \uc2 "As soon as the (long) positions are lightened, I bet \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to prop up the dollar/yen for book closing," said Mitsuo Imaizumi, deputy general manager of the international bond and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  department at Daiwa Securities SMBC.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese corporations close their books for the 2003/04 fiscal year on March 31, and Japan is seen keen to avoid any spike in the yen until then. Such a jump would bite into the overseas earnings of the country's export giants.  \par \par \uc2 The yen also rose against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as sterling, and analysts cited unwinding of high yielding foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated bonds for repatriation ahead of book closing.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was largely unmoved and trading at $1.2255, slightly above late New York levels.  \par \par \uc2 In U.S. trading, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped to a low of $1.2176 , pressured by a steep rise in the yen versus the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The market was also anticipating an announcement following a general council meeting of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to be held in Frankfurt later in the day, to gauge European sentiment following last week's bombings in Madrid.  \par \par \uc2 A suspected al Qaeda-linked car bomb killed 27 people in the heart of Baghdad on Wednesday, but traders said the dollar was moved little by the news. ($1=108.21 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040318e03i0012a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
