\par\par \b \uc2 Yen hits 1-mth high vs dollar as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  tested.  \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 02:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 18 (Reuters) - The yen rose to a one-month high against the dollar on Thursday as foreigners snapped up Tokyo stocks and speculation continued that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be stepping back from aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The yen rose to around 107.15 per dollar above the New York high of 107.95 yen and the highest since February 20.  \par \par \uc2 Riding the same wave, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rose against the euro to a fresh six-week high of 131.45 yen  \par \par \uc2 Traders said they were prepared to buy the yen further on possible signs that the Finance Ministry could be reducing its yen-selling.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "simply out of habit", while Haruhiko Kuroda, special adviser to Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, pointed out that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was only a short-term tool.  \par \par \uc2 "The tone coming from Mr. Tanigaki and Mr. Kuroda was different from what we've been hearing, and (U.S. Treasury Secretary John) Snow declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Junya Tanase, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase.  \par \par \uc2 "These elements are shifting the yen's direction, at least in the short term."  \par \par \uc2 Snow was interviewed on CNBC television on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was trading at $1.2252, slightly above late New York levels. In U.S. trading, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped to a low of $1.2176 pressured by a steep rise in the yen versus the euro.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the market would be focusing on how yen-cross trading would affect the dollar/yen as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to remain supported on recent strength in Tokyo shares.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei average surged to its highest level in nearly two years on Thursday, rising 1.84 percent to 11,647.71 in early trade. Market players suspected foreigners' stock buying was driving the rally.  \par \par \uc2 According to government data released on Thursday, overseas investors continued their buying spree of Japanese stocks last week, purchasing 129.6 billion yen ($1.20 billion) worth.  \par \par \uc2 The market was also anticipating an announcement following a general council meeting of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to be held in Frankfurt later in the day, to gauge European sentiment following last week's bombings in Madrid. ($1=108.21 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040318e03i0006o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
