\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Skids To 1-Mo Low Vs Yen; No Sign Of MOF  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Miyako Takebe  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar crumbled to a one-month low against the yen in Asia Thursday, plowing through key support levels and stop-loss sell orders in the absence of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. hedge funds and other names were cited pushing the dollar through support at Y107.90 and stop-loss triggers in the mid-Y107s, until it came to temporary halt near Y107.10.  \par \par \uc2 Later in the session, a second wave of selling hit the U.S. unit, as those who had gone long dollars expecting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gave up and liquidated their positions. That sent the greenback sliding all the way to Y106.73 - more than one and a half yen down from the morning's high of Y108.38. It was the dollar's weakest level since Feb. 19.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo traders, who said they detected little or no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities, added that without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there would be no significant support levels for the dollar until Y105.16 - its three-year low marked in mid-February.  \par \par \uc2 "No one is interested in buying the dollar/yen in Tokyo right now," said a senior trader at one of Japan's big four banking groups. "Investors just can't feel safe buying dollars when Japan's authorities are taking this sort of stance."  \par \par \uc2 For what it was worth, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pointman repeated Thursday that Tokyo would continue to act when needed in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 "We will continue to (act), although the timing of our action will depend on market conditions," Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 But the words rang hollow as the MOF's lack of action spooked the market.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's sharp rise against the dollar also helped the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen against the euro, as well as other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the pound, the Australian and New Zealand dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The euro/yen cross gave up nearly two yen, as selling dragged it off an intraday high of Y132.75 to a low of Y131.08.  \par \par \uc2 At 0525 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y106.94, below Y108.25 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y108.56 late Wednesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2281, higher than $1.2240 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2265 in Tokyo Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y131.32, down from Y132.47 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y133.15 in Tokyo late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8262, up from $1.8165 in New York and higher than $1.8152 in Tokyo Wednesday. [ 18-03-04 0538GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The dollar later clawed back above Y107 as non-Japanese players sold yen to take profits, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 But as to where the dollar and the yen go from here, "there's only one (market) player that knows the answer to that," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Japanese securities house, referring to MOF, which acts through the Bank of Japan.  \par \par \uc2 Minor chart support for the dollar is expected at Y106.30 - the low for Feb. 19 - although a Tokyo trader noted that chart points haven't been of much use of late as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made the market a "complete mess."  \par \par \uc2 Thursday's lack of action by Japan's authorities gives further credence to the growing view Tokyo is looking for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy exit and is shifting tactics in preparation for when it bows out of the market.  \par \par \uc2 "Given that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a part of the dollar/yen market for well over a year, it's hard to imagine a market in which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't play a part," said Masamichi Koike, head of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp.  \par \par \uc2 But "if the dollar reaches Y105 and there's still no official action, then we may see a dollar freefall which may be rather refreshing in its extremity," Koike said.  \par \par \uc2 Others, however, are still giving the MOF the benefit of the doubt and remain wary of the possibility it may decide to step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  again just before the March 31 end of the fiscal year to help Japanese exporters as they close their books.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \