\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen up vs dollar, euro in test of Tokyo resolve.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases  \par \uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 23:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 17 (Reuters) - The yen hit a three-week high versus the dollar and a six-week peak against the euro on Wednesday amid rising speculation Tokyo may reduce its huge yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 At the same time, international investors looking for low corporate valuations see Japan's rising economic prospects as a good recipe for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, fueling yen demand in order to buy into a strengthening Tokyo stock market. Japan's benchmark Nikkei index closed on Wednesday up 1.73 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "Over the past week, Nikkei is up substantially versus European stocks. Looking forward, Japan is likely to outperform Europe and the United States and for the first time in a long time it looks as if there is an economic recovery in there while valuations are relatively low. That should bring yen strength," said David Durrant, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank Julius Baer in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 0.61 percent to 108.21 yen, above the session nadir of 107.97 yen, its lowest level since Feb. 20 according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fell to a six-week low of 131.71 yen, but rebounded to 132.40 yen, off 0.89 percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 "Europeans have definitely joined in the cross-border equity flow to Japan," said Durrant.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the yen's rise was influenced by former top finance official Eisuke Sakakibara who told Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to end its policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been selling yen for dollars to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for export purposes.  \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara said the United States would not tolerate yen-selling to push the dollar above 115 yen. His comment touched a nerve with investors, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "The one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that's really moving the market is still the yen and the driver is the apparent shift in Japanese policy," said Greg Anderson, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO in Chicago.  \par \par \uc2 The yen also rose against sterling, the Swiss franc and Australian dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fell against the dollar to $1.2235, weighed by the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses against the yen, traders said. Sterling rose to $1.8160.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar slipped briefly against the Swiss franc after an explosion rocked a Baghdad hotel, killing at least 27 people. It then recouped much of its losses to trade nearly unchanged at 1.2768 francs.  \par \par \uc2 BENIGN INFLATION  \par \par \uc2 Generally benign U.S. inflation numbers issued on Wednesday also contributed to dollar weakness by reinforcing the view that U.S. interest rates will remain low for a considerable period, diminishing the appeal of dollar-based assets.  \par \par \uc2 But the inflation data's impact waned as markets focused more on the dollar's movement against the yen.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent half of 2003's record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  total in the first two months of 2004 to prevent the yen from rising against the dollar and crimping Japanese exports by making them too expensive.  \par \par \uc2 Fueling speculation of a shift in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  thinking, Haruhiko Kuroda, a special adviser to Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a short-term policy tool that cannot truly manipulate the world's three major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of vast global capital flows.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility and not intended to depress the yen's value.  \par \par \uc2 "(Breaching) 108.75 yen got us to 108. Any more trial balloons by the (Japanese) \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  about pulling out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take us to 105 in a hurry," said Andrew Busch, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BMO Nesbitt Burns in Chicago. (Additional reporting by Gertrude Chavez in New York).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040317e03h0031n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
