\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar weakens on speculation  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  may end.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 18:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 17 (Reuters) - The dollar dropped against the yen on Wednesday, hurt by growing speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may halt its massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the yen's rise accelerated after former top finance official Eisuke Sakakibara told Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to end its policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been selling yen for dollars to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for export purposes.  \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara said the United States would not tolerate yen-selling to push the dollar above 115 yen. His comment touched a nerve with investors, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "The one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that's really moving the market is still the yen and the driver is the apparent shift in Japanese policy," said Greg Anderson, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro in Chicago.  \par \par \uc2 "If there is really a change in policy on the way, we can expect a move down to 105 yen. But my guess is that the Japanese will probably stop allowing dollar/yen to move much lower once we get to the 108 figure. But I certainly don't throw out the possibility that Japan will decide to get to the 105 floor," he added.  \par \par \uc2 In midday New York trade, the dollar fell 0.66 percent to 108.16 yen after having dropped to a three-week low below 108, according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 The euro also slipped to a six-week low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below 132 yen before trading back up to 132.19 yen, still down over 1 percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 The yen also rose against sterling, the Swiss franc and Australian dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fell against the dollar to $1.2230 , weighed by the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses against the yen, traders said. Sterling was trading higher at $1.8148 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar slipped briefly against the Swiss franc after an explosion in a Baghdad hotel. It then recovered to trade nearly flat at 1.2793 francs .  \par \par \uc2 GREENSPAN SPEAKS  \par \par \uc2 A day after the Federal Open Market Committee kept U.S. interest rates unchanged and expressed more caution about the U.S. labor market, Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan said the U.S. banking system was in good shape to help finance the economic recovery. His comments, however, had little impact on the market.  \par \par \uc2 Generally benign U.S. inflation numbers released earlier in the day also partly weighed on the greenback since the data reinforced the view that U.S. interest rates will remain low for a considerable period, diminishing the appeal of dollar-based assets.  \par \par \uc2 But the inflation data's impact subsequently waned as markets focused more on the dollar's movement against the yen.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent half of last year's record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  total in the first two months of this year to prevent the yen from rising against the dollar and crimping Japanese exports by making them too expensive.  \par \par \uc2 Fueling speculation of a shift in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  thinking, Haruhiko Kuroda, a special adviser to Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a short-term policy tool that cannot truly manipulate the world's three major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of vast global capital flows.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility and not intended to depress the yen's value against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "(Breaching) 108.75 yen got us to 108. Any more trial balloons by the (Japanese) \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  about pulling out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take us to 105 in a hurry," said Andrew Busch, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BMO Nesbitt Burns in Chicago.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040317e03h002hn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
