\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen bounces, boosted by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  doubts.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 762 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds euro zone data, ECB comments, changes byline)  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 17 (Reuters) - The yen hit three-week highs against the dollar and rose one percent to six-week highs against the euro on Wednesday, gripped by speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may scale back its massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A Federal Reserve statement late the previous day left U.S. interest rates unchanged as expected and held out the prospect of no dollar-boosting rise for months to come, leaving the yen to lead the way for the market.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation was building that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be rethinking its policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid worries about losses in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's huge \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the yen's rise was accelerated by remarks from former top finance official Eisuke Sakakibara, who told Reuters it was necessary for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to exit its policy of massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point.  \par \par \uc2 "It seems to be odd timing because we are not yet at the end of the fiscal year but it seems there may have been some internal decision that they want to pull back from the market fairly sharply," said Mitul Kotecha, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Agricole Indosuez.  \par \par \uc2 "That's a good signal to be selling dollar/yen and we're going to see more of that."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell close to 108 yen, notching up losses of 2.5 percent this week, but recovered to 108.46 yen by 1045 GMT, down 0.40 percent from the U.S. close.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fell more than one percent to 132.00 yen its lowest in more than a month, but clawed back to 132.92.  \par \par \uc2 The yen also rose against sterling, the Swiss franc and the Australian dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was steady against the dollar at $1.2258 following the Fed's no-change decision.  \par \par \uc2 Euro zone annual inflation was confirmed at 1.6 percent in February, its lowest since November 1999, though European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief economist Otmar Issing said in a magazine interview no euro zone rate cut was needed to aid sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 "Issing's comments which played down rate cut expectations gave the euro a bit of boost," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland Treasury Services.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. inflation data at 1330 GMT is forecast to show consumer prices rising 0.3 percent on the month in February, with prices excluding volatile food and energy prices up 0.1 percent.  \par \par \uc2 END IN SIGHT?  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already spent half last year's record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  total in the first two months of this year to prevent the yen from rising against the dollar and it succeeded in driving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seven yen lower from a three-year high in mid-February.  \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara said the United States would not tolerate yen-selling to push the yen below 115 yen, a comment which traders said touched a nerve with investors.  \par \par \uc2 Fuelling speculation of a shift in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  thinking, Haruhiko Kuroda, a special adviser to Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a short-term policy tool that cannot truly manipulate the world's three major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of vast global capital flows.  \par \par \uc2 Top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi reiterated on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to dampen volatility.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese corporations close their books for the 2003/04 fiscal year on March 31, and Japan is seen keen to avoid any spike in the yen until then. Such a jump would bite into the overseas earnings of the country's export giants.  \par \par \uc2 PATIENT FED  \par \par \uc2 In the United States the Fed's statement expressed more caution on the economy and noted continued weakness in job creation, which dulled prospects of higher rates any time soon.  \par \par \uc2 Higher rates would make dollar-based assets more attractive to foreign investors. The benchmark official U.S. lending rate stands at 1.0 percent, the lowest since 1958, compared with 4.0 percent in Britain.  \par \par \uc2 Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan is due to speak via satellite on banking to the Independent Community Bankers of America Convention in San Diego at 1630 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, possible sterling-negative impact from minutes of the Bank of England's March policy meeting was counterbalanced by data showing UK unemployment at record lows in the three months to January. The BOE minutes showed an unexpected unanimous vote in favour of steady UK rates in March.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sterling was steady against the dollar  and the euro           ahead of\par the UK's 2004/2005 budget at 1230 GMT.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040317e03h001h7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
