\par\par \b \uc2 Japan officials insist no change in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  policy.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Standing   \par \uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 07:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 17 (Reuters) - Top Japanese finance officials warned markets on Wednesday not to bet on an end to Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has held the yen back against the dollar, reiterating they would act against unwanted volatility.   \par \par \uc2 The yen has risen in recent sessions on speculation \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be rethinking its massive dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of concern over possible losses on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's largest.   \par \par \uc2 But as the yen touched its highest in three weeks against the dollar - bad news for Japan's export-driven recovery - Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki and top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi took aim at anyone tempted to test Tokyo's resolve.   \par \par \uc2 "Our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at curbing volatility in the market and not at directing the yen lower," Tanigaki told a parliamentary committee, repeating Tokyo's usual line.   \par \par \uc2 Speculation over a policy change was triggered by a column in the Nikkei Financial Daily on Tuesday that said some BOJ officials thought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would walk away from large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the end of this month, when the Japanese fiscal year ends.   \par \par \uc2 Market-watchers said they took the report with a pinch of salt, noting that the BOJ merely acts in the market for the government and that the Finance Ministry takes the decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 However the article reflected worries in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which amounted to over 30 trillion yen from January 2003 to February 2004, adding to Japan's pile of public debt.   \par \par \uc2 "There's been a huge change in market sentiment in the last week about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said Jake Moore, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Bank.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts and some politicians have said that Japan could suffer losses on its huge investment in U.S. Treasuries - bought with the dollars bought through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - when U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rates start to rise.   \par \par \uc2 Last week, U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said Japan's economic recovery suggested that Japan was getting closer to a point where large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would no longer meet its monetary policy needs.   \par \par \uc2 STANCE UNCHANGED   \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi told reporters, however, that Japan did not want volatile exchange rates and would continue to act against them.   \par \par \uc2 "Our stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not changed," Mizoguchi told reporters at the ministry. "As the Boca Raton G7 statement said, excess volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is not desirable."   \par \par \uc2 "We will continue to take necessary action against volatility," he said, declining to say whether he thought recent yen moves were sudden.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese corporations close their books for the 2003/04 fiscal year on March 31 and Japan is seen keen to avoid any jump in the yen before then. Such a jump would bite into the overseas earnings of the country's export giants.   \par \par \uc2 Adding to the debate, Haruhiko Kuroda, special adviser to Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said in Washington on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a short-term policy tool that could not control \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.   \par \par \uc2 Traders took his comments as backing up the view that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be reaching the end of its useful life.   \par \par \uc2 For one former MOF official at least, Japan is looking for ways to move away from massive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "Exit policy from fixed exchange rates or massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very difficult, so it is a major task for Mr Mizoguchi and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but I am sure they are considering it," said Eisuke Sakakibara.   \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara, a predecessor to Mizoguchi and once dubbed "Mr Yen" for his influence in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, told Reuters he saw the Japanese authorities allowing the yen to rise slowly.   \par \par \uc2 "For the next two-three months, I think what would happen is a slow appreciation toward 105," he said, adding that the authorities would have to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at times to keep speculators from driving up the yen.   \par \par \uc2 A growing belief among officials that Japan's recovery was sustainable meant the authorities could now tolerate a somewhat stronger yen, he added. (Additional reporting by Linda Sieg, Mariko Hayashibara and David McMahon).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040317e03h000ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
