\b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , touching a two-week high around 132.97 per euro  \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara's comments came after Haruhiko Kuroda, a special adviser to Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a short-term policy tool that cannot truly manipulate the world's three major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of vast global capital flows.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said that even though \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked unsustainable in the longer run, few were ready to aggressively sell the dollar yet.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi reiterated on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to dampen volatility.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the only real support for the dollar right now," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing group at UFJ Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "But even if there were to be a change in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy it would likely be continued until the end of March."  \par \par \uc2 Japanese corporations close their books for the 2003/04 fiscal year on March 31, and Japan is seen keen to avoid any spike in the yen until then. Such a jump would bite into the overseas earnings of the country's export giants.  \par \par \uc2 RATE HIKE HOPES FADES  \par \par \uc2 Also weighing on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the prospect that the U.S. Federal Reserve was in no hurry to raise interest rates anytime soon.  \par \par \uc2 In a statement following its meeting on Tuesday, the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) expressed more caution on the economy, noting continued weakness in job creation, which dulled the prospects of higher rates any time soon.  \par \par \uc2 Such fading prospects of an imminent interest rate rise in the United States prompted many investors to restart buying higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Sterling bounced nearly 2.5 percent against the dollar from the late New York level to around $1.8180 before trimming gains to $1.8145.  \par \par \uc2 Higher rates would make dollar-based assets more attractive to foreign investors. The benchmark official U.S. lending rate stands at 1 percent, the lowest since 1958, compared with 4.0 percent in Britain.  \par \par \uc2 Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan is due to speak via satellite on banking to the Independent Community Bankers of America Convention in San Diego at 1630 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Investors were also awaiting euro zone consumer prices data due at 1000 GMT. Weaker-than-expected data could rekindle market expectations about a rate cut by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The euro was trading at $1.2251/56 compared with its late New York level of around $1.2270.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040317e03h000o4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
