\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar softens on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  doubts, FOMC.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 17 (Reuters) - The dollar slid to new three-week lows against the yen on Wednesday as traders wondered if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would scale-back its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and as the prospect of interest rate hikes in the U.S. faded.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation was building that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be rethinking its policy of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid worries about losses on the world's largest \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, much of which are ploughed into the U.S. Treasury market.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the fall was prompted partly by remarks from former top finance official Eisuke Sakakibara, who told Reuters that it was necessary for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to exit its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy at some point.  \par \par \uc2 "Some investors reacted particularly to the part where he said the U.S. wouldn't tolerate yen-selling to push the yen below 115 yen," said Masamichi Koike, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot trading at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Co.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to 108.53 yen for the first time in three weeks and Tokyo traders said it could briefly test waters below 108 yen. The dollar was around 108.80 yen in late New York on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The yen also edged up against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hovering near two-week highs around 133.30 per euro  \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara's comments came after Harukiko Kuroda, a special adviser to Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a short-term policy tool that cannot truly manipulate the world's three major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of vast global capital flows.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said that even though \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked unsustainable in the longer run, few were ready to aggressively sell the dollar yet.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi reiterated on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to dampen volatility.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the only real support for the dollar right now," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing group at UFJ Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "But even if there were to be a change in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy it would likely be continued until the end of March."  \par \par \uc2 Japanese corporations close their books for the 2003/04 fiscal year on March 31, and Japan is seen keen to avoid any spike in the yen until then. Such a jump would bite into the overseas earnings of the country's export giants.  \par \par \uc2 RATE HIKE HOPES FADES  \par \par \uc2 Also weighing on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the prospect that the U.S. Federal Reserve was in no hurry to raise interest rates anytime soon.  \par \par \uc2 In a statement following its meeting on Tuesday, the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) expressed more caution on the economy, noting continued weakness in job creation, which dulled the prospects of higher rates any time soon.  \par \par \uc2 "I was personally surprised by the wording change as I thought the Fed was trying to let the market prepare for an interest rate hike," said Koike of Sumitomo Mitsui.  \par \par \uc2 Such fading prospects of an imminent interest rate rise in the United States prompted many investors to restart buying higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Sterling bounced nearly 2.5 percent against the dollar from the late New York level to around $1.8180 before trimming gains to $1.8160.  \par \par \uc2 Higher rates would make dollar-based assets more attractive to foreign investors. The benchmark official U.S. lending rate stands at 1 percent, the lowest since 1958, compared with 4.0 percent in Britain.  \par \par \uc2 Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan is due to speak via satellite on banking to the Independent Community Bankers of America Convention in San Diego at 1630 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Investors were also awaiting euro zone consumer prices data due at 1000 GMT. Weaker-than-expected data could rekindle market expectations about a rate cut by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The euro was trading at $1.2273/78 unchanged from the late New York level around $1.2270.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040317e03h000na\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
