\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr/Yen Falls As View Grows MOF May Pull Back  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Miyako Takebe  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar slipped further against the yen in Asia Wednesday, as suspicion in the market grew stronger that Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities may be looking to tone down their aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's overnight fall through Y109.50 - a level traders thought Tokyo would defend - helped back up growing speculation \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is starting to gear up for an eventual end to its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy.  \par \par \uc2 But the greenback's decline was limited as many in the market also still believe the MOF will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the time being - not necessarily to aggressively push the dollar up, but to curb the yen's rise by keeping the dollar's fall gradual, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Driving home that point, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki repeated Wednesday in Parliament that the government will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it feels it needs to "correct excessive fluctuation" in the market.  \par \par \uc2 Other traders said the MOF and BOJ's erratic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions may still be aimed at clearing the market of any form of extreme positioning.  \par \par \uc2 "If authorities are playing the game of 'Punish the Speculator,' as some in the market say, then that would mean the dollar will continue falling until all dollar long positions flee," said Satoshi Tate, vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank.  \par \par \uc2 But Tate added that there seems to be mixed interest for the dollar, given that the mid-Y108s represents good value in the wake of it's rise to Y112 earlier this month, making it difficult to clearly read market positioning.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment toward the dollar was generally weaker after the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee decided overnight to keep interest rates at a 46-year low of 1% and reiterated its stance that inflationary pressures are low enough that it "can be patient in removing its policy accommodation."  \par \par \uc2 Such weakness not only pushed the euro up against the dollar, but also helped high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as sterling, the Australian dollar and the New Zealand dollar recover a bit from the battering they took last week, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y108.56, below Y108.78 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y110.16 late Tuesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2265, higher than $1.2260 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2271 in Tokyo Tuesday. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y133.15, down from Y133.40 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y135.15 in Tokyo late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8152, up from $1.8114 in New York and higher than $1.8040 in Tokyo Tuesday. [ 17-03-04 0543GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The dollar extended its decline against the yen later in the session, falling below Y108.30, partly because the yen drew strength from surging Tokyo share prices.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei 225 Stock Average ended Wednesday up 1.7% at 11436.86, boosted by an overnight rebound on Wall Street, buying by foreign investors and continued hopes for Japan's economic recovery. The Topix index ended up 1.9% at 1141.71, marking its highest close since August 2001.  \par \par \uc2 An apparent lack of official support as the dollar extended its slide in the afternoon also fanned speculation aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not appear until the dollar falls significantly further.  \par \par \uc2 "Some are starting to say the MOF might not come in until Y105," said a senior trader at a Japanese brokerage. But he was quick to point out that those same people were likely the ones who until recently were convinced Japanese authorities were aiming to lift the dollar back up around Y115. "There are a lot of speculators out there."  \par \par \uc2 The strong stock market performance also helped the yen advance against the euro. The euro/yen cross tumbled late in the Asian session, triggering massive stop-loss sell orders at Y133.00 and then Y132.80 on its way down to a low of Y132.55. The pair's fall also pulled the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 17-03-04 0646GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2