\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar weakens vs yen but steady vs euro after Fed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases  \par \uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 22:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Recasts lead, adds comment, updates with late New York prices)   \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 16 (Reuters) - The dollar fell steeply against the yen but held nearly unchanged versus the euro on Tuesday, influenced more by market positioning and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues than by the Fed's decision not to raise interest rates.   \par \par \uc2  In its post-meeting statement, the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy-setting committee expressed more caution on the economy, noting continued weakness in job creation, which dulled the prospects of higher U.S. interest rates any time soon.   \par \par \uc2  Higher rates would make dollar-based assets more attractive to foreign investors. The benchmark official U.S. lending rate stands at 1 percent, a 1958 low.   \par \par \uc2  But the Fed did reiterate a balanced outlook on inflation and growth.   \par \par \uc2  "The dollar gyrated up and down after the statement because the Fed seemed to go out of their way to express a balance of risks, leaving the dollar little changed after all," Daniel Tenengauzer, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers in New York. "The market positioned itself for this decision."   \par \par \uc2  The euro first rose on the Fed's decision before quickly losing ground. It hit a session low around $1.2239 , according to Reuters data, before climbing back to just under the unchanged mark of $1.2271.   \par \par \uc2  "With U.S. rates set to remain low for months to come and U.S. yields remaining relatively unattractive ... this should be supportive for the euro versus the dollar," said Rebecca Patterson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase in New York. Patterson said topside resistance for the euro is around $1.2385.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar was already down sharply against the yen on market speculation the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be poised to cut back on its large yen-selling/dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from plunging by steadily buying dollars to offset speculative selling of greenbacks and to keep the yen from strengthening and crimping Japanese exports.   \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials denied any change in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, although a comment by Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui that irregular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves had abated was seen by some as indicating a more relaxed stance on the yen's strength.   \par \par \uc2  Japan's Nikkei Financial Daily reported late on Monday, New York time, that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may stop \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) isn't there, so the dollar's going to fall," said Ralph DelZenero, vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank One in Chicago. "Markets are trying to see what's down there and they're not seeing Japanese names. They think the dollar is worth closer to 100 yen than 110," he added.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was responding to domestic policy concerns through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the negative impact a stronger yen has on falling domestic prices, Haruhiko Kuroda, special adviser to Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said in Washington on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  Kuroda added that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a short-term policy tool which cannot truly manipulate the world's three major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of vast global capital flows.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to a three-week low of 108.65 yen after the Fed's announcement before climbing back to 108.89 yen , a loss of 1.23 percent on the day according to Reuters data. The euro dropped to 133.33 yen , off 1.50 percent before drifting back to 133.54 yen, still a loss of 1.32 percent.   \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the euro rose versus the dollar despite an unexpectedly sharp fall in German investor expectations.   \par \par \uc2  Germany's ZEW institute said its gauge of economic expectations fell in March, for the third straight month, to its lowest level since last summer. It blamed the fall on concerns over the pace of Europe's economic recovery, particularly after last week's deadly bombings in Madrid.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040316e03g0031d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
