\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar weakens further as Fed stands pat on rates.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases   \par \uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 21:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with Fed, updates prices, adds comment, changes byline)   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 16 (Reuters) - An already weak dollar fell further on Tuesday after the U.S. Federal Reserve left interest rates unchanged and indicated more caution on the U.S. economy, diminishing prospects of a dollar-positive interest rate hike.   \par \par \uc2 In its post-meeting statement, the Fed note continuing weakness in U.S. job creation, which has dulled the prospect of higher interest rates any time soon.   \par \par \uc2 Higher rates would make dollar-based assets more attractive to foreign investors.   \par \par \uc2 "With U.S. rates set to remain low for months to come and U.S. yields remaining relatively unattractive ... this should be supportive for the euro versus the dollar," said Rebecca Patterson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase in New York.   \par \par \uc2 The euro bounced up and down after the Fed's statement, trading to a session low around $1.2239 , according to Reuters data, before climbing back to the unchanged mark of $1.2271. Patterson said topside resistance for the euro is around $1.2385.   \par \par \uc2 "Recall that in the last statement the Fed said other indicators are leading to an improvement in the labor market. The Fed has dropped that completely and now all they're saying is that the labor market is lagging ... So this statement is mainly dollar-negative," said Richard Franulovich, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac Banking Corp in New York.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar was already down sharply against the yen on market speculation the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be poised to cut back on its large yen-selling/dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the dollar from plunging by being a steady buyer of dollars to offset speculative selling of greenbacks and keep the yen from strengthening.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials denied any change in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, although a comment by Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui that irregular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves had abated was interpreted by some as indicating a more relaxed stance on the yen's strength.   \par \par \uc2 Japan's Nikkei Financial Daily reported late on Monday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may stop \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The BOJ (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) isn't there, so the dollar's going to fall," said Ralph DelZenero, vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank One in Chicago. "Markets are trying to see what's down there and they're not seeing Japanese names. They think the dollar is worth closer to 100 yen than 110," he added.   \par \par \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda, special adviser to Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said in Washington on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was responding to domestic policy concerns through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the negative impact a stronger yen has on falling domestic prices.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to three-week lows against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Fed announcement, hitting 108.65 yen , a loss of 1.45 percent on the day according to Reuters data. The euro dropped to 133.33 yen , off 1.50 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The euro gained from the dollar's weakness, shrugging off an unexpectedly sharp fall in German investor expectations.   \par \par \uc2 Germany's ZEW institute said its gauge of economic expectations fell in March, for the third straight month, to its lowest level since last summer. It blamed the fall on concerns over the pace of Europe's economic recovery, particularly after last week's deadly bombings in Madrid.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar traded at 1.2777 francs , down 0.20 percent while sterling rose 0.34 percent to $1.8116.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040316e03g002ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
