\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr/Yen Down; Questions About Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Stance  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 1,120 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar slipped against the yen in Asia Tuesday, weighed by continued speculation Japan may be examining backing away from its aggressive yen-selling campaign.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback was still reeling after an overnight tumble, caused in part by a report in the Nikkei Financial Daily that the Bank of Japan may be weighing an exit strategy for its yen-weakening market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo players were divided on how to interpret the report, which said some BOJ officials were predicting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will walk away from its huge yen-selling campaign by the end of this month.  \par \par \uc2 But the report kept the greenback's topside heavy after it made a sudden 35-sen fall to around Y110.03, which some traders attributed to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulling bids around Y110.30.  \par \par \uc2 "Some suspicious bids around Y110.30 were pulled out, but the usual names (acting as an agent for the MOF) came in to support the dollar when it fell near Y110.00," a dealer at a European bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro also fell against the yen in early trade on large-scale offers placed by a U.S. investment bank, dragging the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down against the dollar along the way, the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 But the euro mostly recouped its losses against the dollar later in the day as traders moved to cover short positions, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ board's decision to keep monetary policy unchanged Tuesday had little impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates as it was largely expected amid growing signs of recovery in the Japanese economy and recent stability in financial markets.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y110.16, below Y110.30 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y110.91 late Monday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2271, largely unchanged from $1.2272 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $1.2232 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y135.15, down from Y135.40 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y135.71 in Tokyo late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8040, down from $1.8055 in New York but higher than $1.8008 in Tokyo Monday. [ 16-03-04 0544GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki was quick to play down the Nikkei report, stressing that there has been no change in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy of taking action against moves out of line with economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 "I won't comment on daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, but our stance remains unchanged," Tanigaki told reporters. "We believe \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should move stably in reflection of (economic) fundamentals."  \par \par \uc2 The report comes in the wake of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities in recent weeks as the March 31 fiscal-year end approaches. Japan has sold Y10 trillion in the first two months of 2004 alone after selling a record Y20 trillion in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 While most market participants believe the ministry won't stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet, some think the BOJ may be sending up a trial balloon to see how the market would respond to hints of a more relaxed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance ahead.  \par \par \uc2 "A well-known Japanese paper like the Nikkei Financial Daily won't write stories like this without paying due heed to the views of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities," the European bank dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Ryohei Muramatsu, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Commerzbank's Tokyo branch, said the significance of the report lies in the fact that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's media, which have remained generally supportive of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are finally beginning to publish stories critical of the ministry's yen-selling campaign.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF will have to look at changing its heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance at some point, but that won't be easy, Muramatsu said.  \par \par \uc2 "The yen-buying magma is red hot, so the dollar may tumble near Y105 and then test further lows" once the MOF exits its heavy-handed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign, Muramatsu said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 16-03-04 0643GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki was quick to play down the Nikkei report, stre