\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Tanigaki: No Change To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Policy  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Miyako Takebe  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 05:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki Tuesday held firm his resolve to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets despite a media report that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is looking for a way to end its massive yen-selling campaign.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki said Japan's policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't changed and it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever the yen moves out of line with economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 "I won't comment on daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, but our stance remains unchanged," Sadakazu Tanigaki told reporters. "We believe \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should move stably in reflection of (economic) fundamentals."  \par \par \uc2 His comments follow a plunge in the dollar's exchange rate against the yen to a two-week low of Y109.25 in New York trading Monday after the Nikkei Financial Daily reported "some central banks officials" in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expecting "large-scale" yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease after the end of this month.  \par \par \uc2 Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , acting through the Bank of Japan, then pulled the greenback above Y110.00, traders said. Market participants generally think Japanese monetary authorities want the dollar above Y110.00 on March 31, which marks Japan's fiscal year end.  \par \par \uc2 The report comes in the wake of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese monetary authorities in recent weeks as the March 31 fiscal-year end approaches. Japan has sold Y10 trillion in the first two months of 2004 alone after selling a record Y20 trillion in 2003  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki said the MOF "will continue to take appropriate action in the event there are excessive moves."  \par \par \uc2 Traders and strategists played down the Nikkei report, saying that they don't expect the Finance Ministry to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet.  \par \par \uc2 Still, one brokerage trader said exporters and institutional investors may be tempted to unwind long dollar positions following the report.  \par \par \uc2 Strategists say Japan remains keen to discourage speculators from taking big positions in the market, that helped push the dollar to a three-year low of Y105.16 last month.  \par \par \uc2 "The Japanese authorities' intention is to get rid of speculators," said Mitsuo Imaizumi, deputy general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Daiwa Securities SMBC.  \par \par \uc2 Others said that the report only noted dissatisfaction among officials at the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  about recent heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and didn't mention views of officials at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is set.  \par \par \uc2 "While its clear that some within the BOJ have reservations about the yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, this doesn't by itself mean that the dollar/yen will be allowed to fall, as was evident in dollar/yen price action overnight," said UBS in a morning research note.  \par \par \uc2 "The MOF is ultimately responsible for yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and hence the market will place particular importance on comments by MOF officials for any signs that they might relax on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," UBS added.  \par \par \uc2 At 0411 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y110.14.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Takashi Nakamichi contributed to this story).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson [ 16-03-04 0427GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040316e03g00040\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
