\par\par \b \uc2 Japan MOF Mizoguchi: Excess  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Volatility Inappropriate  \b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 01:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's basic stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains unchanged, Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Tuesday, underscoring that the authorities will take action against any sharp rise in the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "We will take action depending on market conditions at the time," Zembei Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters when he arrived at the ministry.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi was speaking after the dollar dropped to a two-week low of Y109.25 in New York overnight on a column in the Nikkei Financial Daily that said "some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials" in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expecting the nation's "large-scale" yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease after the end of this month.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose back above Y110.00 on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said, and at 0052 GMT Tuesday the greenback was trading around Y110.20 in Tokyo. [ 16-03-04 0101GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi declined to comment on the dollar's broad decline against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight, saying it was inappropriate to comment on daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate moves.  \par \par \uc2 He also said he "didn't know" whether signs al-Qaida may have been behind Thursday's train bombings in Madrid had caused the dollar's overnight drop.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves on various factors, but excess volatility and disorderly movements (in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates) are inappropriate," as the Group of Seven major industrialized nations agreed at their meeting in Boca Raton, Florida last month, Mizoguchi said.  \par \par \uc2 "We will cope with individual (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market) situations based on this understanding," he said, suggesting that further yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be justified if it's aimed at countering excessive rises in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi declined to comment on a column in a major U.S. economic magazine that criticized \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and called him "Mr. Dollar" for his central role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "They haven't heard my side of the story, so I won't comment on this," Mizoguchi said.  \par \par \uc2 The column in the latest issue of BusinessWeek, titled "Don't Let 'Mr. Dollar' Get Away With It," sarcastically depicts Mizoguchi as "a faceless bureaucrat" in Tokyo but a "celebrity" in global foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for his seemingly endless purchase of the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 It concludes by urging the G7 countries' financial officials to do "some serious arm-twisting" so that "Mr. Dollar (will) let the free market be free."  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie and Alastair Gale [ 16-03-04 0146GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040316e03g0000v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
