\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar stumbles as market ponders life without BOJ.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 471 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 14:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 16 (Reuters) - The dollar fell across the board on Tuesday, yielding almost one percent to the yen after an influential newspaper said Tokyo could end its policy of selling yen for dollars by the end of the month.  \par \par \uc2 A weaker than expected German economic sentiment survey took a back seat as the market focused on the article in the Nikkei Financial Daily and looked ahead to a U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make a statement at 1915 GMT and is universally expected to keep interest rates at a 46-year low of 1.0 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "The wording of the Fed statement may be interesting but the big story at the moment is Japan," said Jesper Dannesboe, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein.  \par \par \uc2 "The market senses Japan may soon allow dollar/yen to trade lower so we have seen knee-jerk selling of dollars."  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei report suggested \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could walk away from large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the end of this month.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials denied any change in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy though a comment by Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui that irregular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves had abated was interpreted by some as indicating a more relaxed stance on the yen's strength.  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tokyo trade but the effect was short-lived and, by 1240 GMT, the dollar had fallen back near session lows of 109.24 yen.  \par \par \uc2 DISMAL ZEW  \par \par \uc2 The euro also took advantage of the dollar's weakness, rising 0.6 percent to $1.2354 and shrugging off news of an unexpectedly sharp fall in German investor expectations.  \par \par \uc2 Germany's ZEW institute said its monthly gauge of economic expectations fell to 57.6 in March, its lowest since last August. It blamed the fall on concerns over the pace of Europe's economic recovery, particularly after last week's bombings in Madrid.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Tuesday the BOJ kept its monetary policy unchanged, taking heart from mounting evidence of an economic pick up.  \par \par \uc2 Separately it also kept its economic assessment unchanged in a monthly report, saying the economy was in a gradual recovery.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei article had resonance coming after recent comments from Federal Reserve chairman Alan Greenspan that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic recovery may make yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  harder to justify.  \par \par \uc2 Keen to shore up its export-led recovery, Japan has poured more than 10 trillion yen ($91.44 billion) into \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the first two months of this year.  \par \par \uc2 "The market had viewed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an ongoing policy tool, not a temporary measure," said Shahab Jalinoos, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO.  \par \par \uc2 "The report questions this understanding and has sent the dollar lower."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040316e03g001u0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
