\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slips as investors ponder yen without BOJ.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki  \par \uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 10:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 16 (Reuters) - The dollar fell towards the previous day's two-week low against the yen on Tuesday after an influential newspaper said Tokyo could end its aggressive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy by the end of March.  \par \par \uc2 A report in the Nikkei Financial Daily centring on comments by a senior Bank of Japan official also said some central bankers were predicting upward pressure on the yen would abate from April.  \par \par \uc2 Officials denied any change in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, with finance minister Sadakazu Tanigaki and top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi repeating Japan will act against sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo dealers saw Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift the dollar earlier, backing their words with action. But the effect was short-lived and the dollar slipped to 109.55 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's losses against the yen lifted the euro on the greenback before Germany's ZEW economic sentiment index at 1000 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 "The market showed a knee-jerk reaction. Obviously \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in this scale can't go on indefinitely. They are subsidising the manufacturing sector at the expense of consumers, preventing the corporate sector from adjusting and becoming competitive," said Mary Davis, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston.  \par \par \uc2 "The ZEW index should reflect signals the euro zone economy is a bit weaker than before."  \par \par \uc2 By 0845 GMT the dollar stood near the day's lows. Against the euro it had fallen half a percent on the day to $1.2345 before inching up to $1.2336.  \par \par \uc2 The ZEW index is forecast to slip to 66.0 in March from 69.9 in February, registering the third consecutive fall on the month. The ZEW institute said Thursday's bombings in Madrid will probably affect the poll results as about 40 percent of 300 or so responses were to be returned between Thursday and Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve holds a one-day meeting on interest rate policy and a statement is expected at 1915 GMT, when it is expected to hold rates steady.  \par \par \uc2 EXIT STRATEGY?  \par \par \uc2 Japanese monetary authorities have already spent more than 10 trillion yen in the first two months this year, half of the annual record spent last year. The BOJ acts as an agent bank for the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The Nikkei story planted a seed of doubt in the market as everyone was convinced that the (Japanese authorities) could do what it wanted," said Peter Fontaine, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at KBC in Brussels. "It's not a one-way bet that the Bank has won a battle by propping dollar/yen up. There is an underlying case to be made for a strengthening yen as we see the Japanese economy pick up a bit."  \par \par \uc2 The article comes after Fed chairman Alan Greenspan said earlier this month Japan's economic recovery may soon no longer justify its large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold the yen down.  \par \par \uc2 Greenspan also said Asian central banks' purchases of U.S. dollar assets resulting from their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been extraordinary and, in the case of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , awesome.  \par \par \uc2 "If they continue to prevent their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from reaching an equilibrium then they will be introducing distortion in the domestic and international market mechanism," Davis said.  \par \par \uc2 BOJ governor Toshihiko Fukui said irregular moves are abating and Economics and Financial Services minister Heizo Takenaka said the yen's rise has halted.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Tuesday the BOJ kept its monetary policy unchanged, taking heart from mounting evidence of an economic pick up, a recent fall in the yen against the dollar and receding worries about the financial system.  \par \par \uc2 Separately it also kept its economic assessment unchanged in a monthly report, saying the economy was in a gradual recovery.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040316e03g0017e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
