\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar steadies vs yen after rollercoaster ride.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Naomi Tajitsu   \par \uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 07:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 16 (Reuters) - The dollar steadied against the yen on Tuesday after erratic trade that saw the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spike up on suspected Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid talk Tokyo may consider scaling back yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The dollar shot up more than a quarter yen to around 110.38 yen in early trading after tumbling to the day's low of 110.03 yen on a Nikkei Financial Daily report that the government could end its aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.   \par \par \uc2 In New York trading, the report had pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down to a two-week low of 109.20 yen before marking 110.28/33 in late trade.   \par \par \uc2 At 0220 GMT, the dollar had steadied somewhat, trading at 110.09 yen .   \par \par \uc2 "The market is trying to find out what officials plan to do about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jun Kitazawa, assistant vice president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section at Brown Brothers Harriman in Tokyo.   \par \par \uc2 "Since this is the only thing that is keeping up dollar/yen, if they do scale back, the dollar will fall."   \par \par \uc2 Some saw the dollar's drop to just above the psychologically important 110-yen level as a deliberate test for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF).   \par \par \uc2 "The drop was designed as a market attempt to challenge MOF resolve," said Naomi Fink, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas.   \par \par \uc2 As if to underscore the government's determination to continue its policy, the dollar rebounded just as Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said there had been no change in Japan's belief that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should reflect economic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 "I am not going to comment on day-to-day moves. But there is no change in our basic stance," he said, addressing the dollar's slide in overnight trading.   \par \par \uc2 "We are maintaining our policy of taking appropriate action when there are abrupt movements (in the yen)," he added.   \par \par \uc2 MIZOGUCHI WEIGHS IN   \par \par \uc2 Top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi also reiterated his usual line, saying the Japanese government would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when it saw the need.   \par \par \uc2 "The market moves on various factors but our view is unchanged from what was said at (the G7 meeting in) Boca Raton, and that excessive volatility and disorderly moves are not appropriate," he told reporters.   \par \par \uc2 "Basically we will act along those lines."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record 20 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003. It has already spent another 10 trillion in the first two months of this year in dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  that dealers suspect have become a common and often sustained market occurence.   \par \par \uc2 Market players suspect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped catapult the dollar to five-month highs above 112 yen last week, up more than six percent from 3-= year lows near 105 yen ploughed last month.   \par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the dollar remained firm ahead of a meeting of the Federal Open Market Committee later in the day, during which the body is expected to say it can be patient in removing its accommodative policy.   \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2252/56 versus 1.2265/69.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Tokyo traders anticipated the market would remain volatile for the rest of the day and expected the dollar/yen to be pinned down by Japan for the time being.   \par \par \uc2 "We might see increased volatility because of the overnight drop and we'll see more attempts to challenge MOF resolve," said Paribas' Fink.   \par \par \uc2 "But being the financial year-end, it's likely that MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue in the short-term." ((Reporting by Kazunori Takada and Naomi Tajitsu; Editing by Brent Kininmont; Reuters messaging; naomi.tajitsu.reuters.com@reuters.net; Tel +81-3-3432-8657))    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  ..        Debt...      Indicators...\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par  \par All spots  Tokyo spots        Europe spots        Volatilities\par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par  \par   World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par   Official rates...\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par   Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par   Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040316e03g000sq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
