\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Japan denies changes in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  policy as yen rises.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Chisa Fujioka  \par \uc2 704 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 10:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 16 (Reuters) - Japanese officials sought on Tuesday to brush aside growing speculation that they could soon scale back their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , aimed at preventing a higher yen from derailing an economic recovery.   \par \par \uc2  As they spoke the dollar spiked up against the yen - a move that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders suspected was due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities to make a point about their determination - although the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  faltered again later in the day.   \par \par \uc2  Asked about the yen's renewed rise, Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki told reporters: "I am not going to comment on day-to-day moves. But there is no change in our basic stance.   \par \par \uc2  "We are maintaining our policy of taking appropriate actions when there are abrupt movements (in the yen)."   \par \par \uc2  Tanigaki was speaking only hours after the dollar fell more than one percent against the yen in Monday's New York trading on a newspaper article saying the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was weighing an exit strategy for its yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The renewed yen rise comes after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's huge yen-selling, which totalled a record 20 trillion yen ($181 billion) last year and 10 trillion yen in just the first two months of this year, raised eyebrows in markets and among global policymakers.   \par \par \uc2  Last week, U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said Japan's economic recovery suggested that Japan was getting closer to a point where large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would no longer meet the country's monetary policy needs.   \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Toshihiko Fukui said on Tuesday, however, that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary easing stance.   \par \par \uc2  "Monetary policy is being conducted to the fullest so that deflation is overcome and the economy improves," Fukui told a news conference after a BOJ Policy Board meeting, at which monetary policy was left unchanged.   \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ believes that in that kind of situation, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market does not contradict the direction of policy."   \par \par \uc2  IF NEED BE   \par \par \uc2  Tanigaki's deputy on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi, reiterated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it saw the need.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar last month halted a two-year bear trend thanks to the heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bouncing from 3-1/2-year lows around 105.10 yen to reach five-month highs around 112.35 yen last week.   \par \par \uc2  But it has since slipped, falling towards 109.50 yen on Tuesday despite a brief quarter percent spike-up earlier in the day from around 110 yen on what traders suspected was continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry officials close to market activity were not immediately available to confirm whether they had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The dollar's drop on Monday was fuelled by an article in the Nikkei Financial Daily that said some BOJ officials thought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would walk away from large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the end of this month, when the current fiscal year finishes.   \par \par \uc2  The article - a column based on comments by an unnamed BOJ official - ran in Tuesday's edition, but an English translation was published during Monday's New York trading hours.   \par \par \uc2  Although the BOJ merely acts as an agent bank for the government, whose Finance Ministry makes decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the article fuelled speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon scale back its yen-selling.   \par \par \uc2  Market-watchers said they took the report with a grain of salt.   \par \par \uc2  "The article alludes to concerns of the sustainability of JPY (yen) sales at the current pace. Clearly no \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to be involved in such a one-sided market, and would feel uncomfortable with the recent pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Greg Gibbs, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBC Capital Markets in Sydney.   \par \par \uc2  "But overall, with few other policy options, they are unlikely to be considering a free float any time soon. It might however, revert to allowing modest JPY strength in the context of building economic recovery."   \par \par \uc2  He added that since Japan's interest rates, already virtually zero, could not be reduced further, the authorities were unlikely to ditch \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was tied to their anti-deflation policy, in the near term. ($1=110.32 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040316e03g0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\p