\par\par \b \uc2 ODJ Debt Futures Review: Near Steady Amid Offsetting Factors  \b0\par\par\uc2 954 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 21:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -- Weaker Stock Market, Terror Concerns Are Supportive For Bonds \par   -- Industrial Production, Reports About BOJ Cited As Bearish Factors \par  \par By Allen Sykora \par     Chicago, March 15 (OsterDowJones) - Interest-rate futures on Monday found \par themselves sandwiched between several bullish and bearish factors, analysts \par reported. As a result, they ended up pretty much where they left off on Friday. \par     Supportive factors included a selloff in equities and continued \par uneasiness about terrorism, as reports suggest increasingly that al-Qaida may \par have played a role in last week's train-bombing attacks in Spain. However, the \par upside in bonds was blocked by a strong report on industrial production and \par reports that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is mulling the possibility of scaling back its \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts. \par     "We haven't had a big move, but it was an interesting day," said Lara \par Akin, financial futures analyst with Refco.com. \par     Jun 10-year notes settled down 3.5 ticks 115-22.5, Jun Treasury bonds were \par unchanged at 114-30 and Sep Eurodollars were steady at 98.675. \par     "It's a tug-of-war," said Richard Heyboer, account executive with Fox \par Investments, a division of Man Financial. "The selloff in equities is putting \par some upside pressure on the bonds." \par     As the interest-rate futures pits were closing, the Dow industrials were \par down by around 95 to 100 points and the Nasdaq was down by roughly 35 points. \par     "But we had some news with the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saying they may stay out of \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Heyboer. \par     In its Tuesday editions, the Nikkei Financial Daily said that Japanese \par officials are looking for an exit strategy for its yen-weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par efforts. \par     "Some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials predict that it will walk away from large- \par scale \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the end of this month and that the upward pressure on \par the yen, even without such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -boosting measures, will abate beginning in \par April," the newspaper reported. Japan's fiscal year ends on March 31. \par     For some time now, the BOJ has been an active buyer of the U.S. dollar in \par an effort to keep the yen from getting too muscular and hurting the country's \par export-oriented economy. When the BOJ buys dollars through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , they tend to get recycled into government securities. Thus, the \par curtailment of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would remove one of the factors that has been \par supporting the Treasury market lately. \par     Debt futures could be ready to back down from the levels they had climbed \par to in recent weeks, said Heyboer. \par     "But with the terrorism fears, everybody has got one finger on the buy \par trigger right now," he added. \par     A senior Spanish anti-terrorism investigator has said "the weight of \par evidence" points to al-Qaida for the train-bombing attacks that killed 200 \par people last week. The group has issued an apparent further claim of \par responsibility and a man with links to al-Quaida has been jailed in Spain. \par     Early this morning, contacts cited that focus on terrorism as the main \par factor that enabled debt futures to open the day with a bid. \par     "Then the industrial-production numbers came out pretty strong and caused \par a nice little sell-off in early trade," said Akin. "Then terror took effect \par and we traded back up higher. But then around the lunchtime hour, we had a \par spike downward because there were some wire reports saying the BOJ was \par considering cutting back \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and were going cold turkey. So the bond \par market got clobbered on the news." \par     Not long afterward, however, there were reports that the BOJ was \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again, she added. "So we kind of headed back up to where we were \par before that news broke." \par     The bonds and 10-year notes are essentially in the fourth day of sideways \par trading, said Heyboer. "So you could make a case for a move in either \par direction right now," he added. \par     Akin put support in Jun 10-year notes around 15-18, which was the session \par low on two of the last three trading days. Initial resistance was pegged at \par Friday's open-outcry high of 116-07. \par     Support in Jun Treasury bonds was put around 114-17 to 114-19. Akin listed \par resistance around 115-15. \par     The Federal Open Market Committee is scheduled to hold its second meeting \par of 2004 Tuesday. No change in interest rates is expected, and most analysts \par and economists say they do not look for the Fed to materially change its post- \par meeting statement from Jan. 28, when officials said they can be "patient" with \par accommodative policy. A statement is normally released after meetings around \par 1315 CT (1915 GMT). \par     "I don't think they're going to say anything new or different," said \par Akin. "But we have seen huge moves (in the past) on one word that everyone \par knew they were going to say beforehand." \par     In Sep Eurodollars, she put support at 98.65 and resistance at 98.70. \par     "If the Fed changes anything at all to look closer to tightening, I think \par it's going to go down to the mid 98.50s that we had seen before the (February) \par payroll number," said Akin. \par     As for Monday's main economic data, the Federal Reserve said that \par industrial production rose 0.7% during February, while capacity utilization \par rose to 76.6% from 76.1% in January. Consensus forecasts had been for a rise \par of 0.3% or 0.4% in production, with capacity utilization of 76.4%. \par     February housing starts are due out Tuesday at 0730 CT (1330 GMT). \par Expectations are for an annualized rate of 1.93 million to 1.94 million units. \par   --- \par Allen Sykora, OsterDowJones \par sykora@bendcable.com \par Copyright 2004 OsterDowJones Commodity News (ODJ). All rights reserved. \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-15-04 1537ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 61060  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCS000020040315e03f000pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
