\par\par \b \uc2 Update 1-U.S. Treasury says no change in dollar policy.  \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 21:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, March 15 (Reuters) - A Treasury Department spokesman on Monday said U.S. policy in support of a strong dollar was unchanged and declined comment on reports \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might trim its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "There is no change in our strong-dollar policy," Treasury spokesman Rob Nichols said at a weekly briefing for reporters.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. policy also holds that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by governments - large-scale buying or selling of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to affect their relative values - should be kept to a minimum.  \par \par \uc2 Nichols declined to comment on a report by Japanese economic daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might cut its large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is aimed at keeping the yen's value from rising.  \par \par \uc2 "We don't comment on specific market activity by foreign governments," Nichols said. The Japanese newspaper said many BOJ officials were questioning the policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by selling yen to buy tens of billions of dollars to keep the yen's value weaker.  \par \par \uc2 "Some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials predict that it will walk away from large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the end of this month and that the upward pressure on the yen ... will abate beginning in April," the Nikkei reported.  \par \par \uc2 On other topics, Nichols said Treasury Secretary John Snow had been invited to meet the presidents of the 12 regional Federal Reserve banks, which make up the U.S. Federal Reserve system.  \par \par \uc2 Nichols said Snow and the Fed officials would hold a "social dinner" on Monday night and they would discuss current economic conditions among other topics.  \par \par \uc2 The Fed's policy-setting Federal Open Market Committee meets on Tuesday to plot interest-rate strategy for the period ahead, amid universal expectation it will leave its key federal funds rate at 1 percent, its lowest level since 1958.  \par \par \uc2 . (C) Reuters Limited 2004.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040315e03f002tp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
