\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Up Vs Yen, Euro On Position Adjustments  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Miyako Takebe  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 07:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar rose against the yen and the euro in Asia Friday, as position adjustments and its strength against the Australian dollar helped it shake off some of its overnight bearishness.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit fell overnight amid fears al-Qaida may have been behind Madrid bombings. But it recovered the Y111-mark in Asia Friday, helped by yen-selling caused by a slide in the Nikkei 225 Stock Average, which lost as much as 1.8% at one point.  \par \par \uc2 However, most of the dollar's movements against the yen were dictated by position adjustments by investors unwilling to take large risks in the wake of recent suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities, Tokyo traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have put short-term speculators out of commission and to have sapped their energy to make large bets," said Masamichi Koike, head of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp.  \par \par \uc2 Position adjustments sparked by the dollar's surge to a fresh three-month high against the Australian dollar also helped the greenback gain ground against the euro, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Driving the U.S. dollar's strength against the Australian dollar was the continuing unwinding of carry trades - borrowing of low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy assets in higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - due to the shifting outlook for interest rates and the brighter outlook for the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y111.03, above Y110.90 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y110.57 late Thursday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2281, lower than $1.2347 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $1.2208 in Tokyo Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y136.39, down from Y136.93 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y134.96 in Tokyo late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.7961, down from $1.8111 in New York and lower than $1.8007 in Tokyo Thursday. [ 12-03-04 0608GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Unwinding of yen carry trades also hurt the euro/yen cross, keeping the European unit broadly subdued during the Asian session, traders said  \par \par \uc2 Possibly foreshadowing further weakness in the euro, major investment banks have begun to warn against growing weakness in the euro-zone economies, and have cut their near-term forecasts for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs, in research report, lowered its three-month forecast for the euro to $1.20 from $1.26, saying the trend in the euro zone's broad balance of payments appears to be deteriorating, while domestic demand struggles. It added that its own estimate of the euro's fair value would be around $1.15, although it stuck to a six- and twelve-month forecast of $1.30.  \par \par \uc2 Also in a research report, Morgan Stanley cut its end-June forecast for the euro to $1.19 from $1.25, saying that the European Union economies, especially that of Germany, aren't nearly as robust as many had initially thought.  \par \par \uc2 "Understanding the risks to the outlook, European policymakers are likely to become more vigilant in guarding the $1.30 or the $1.35 line than the market things," Morgan Stanley said in the report. "We believe it will be extremely difficult for the euro/dollar to test $1.30 again this year."  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 12-03-04 0650GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040312e03c0006h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
