\par\par \b \uc2 TECHNICALS- \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  market views and key levels.  \b0\par\par\uc2 865 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 18:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     NEW YORK, March 11 (Reuters) - Following is a selection of\par comments from analysts on important technical developments in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     SHAUN OSBORNE, CHIEF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STRATEGIST, SCOTIA CAPITAL:\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - EURO/DOLLAR: "The euro remains vulnerable to further  \f28 \par \par \uc2 losses. Whilst holding below the $1.2330-$1.2340 gap was noted  \par \par \uc2 yesterday, we will need to see the euro close through $1.2450  \par \par \uc2 before we can be more confident of sustainable gains. Support  \par \par \uc2 below the market is at $1.2130-$1.2150, then $1.2060."  \par \par \uc2 - DOLLAR/YEN: "Suggested yesterday that the choppy trade  \par \par \uc2 in recent days may prompt some pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to revise  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and the close under 111 yen yesterday would  \par \par \uc2 indicate that we may be seeing the Japanese monetary  \par \par \uc2 authorities dial back the aggression to some degree at least.  \par \par \uc2 Support now expected at 110 yen - coincident with what should  \par \par \uc2 be strong technical support at 110.00-110.20 yen. Below here  \par \par \uc2 would be significant from a chart point of view. While  \par \par \uc2 dollar/yen looks technically overextended and ripe for a  \par \par \uc2 correction, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to remain a factor in the  \par \par \uc2 short run."  \par \par \uc2 - U.S. DOLLAR/CANADIAN DOLLAR: "The Canadian dollar  \par \par \uc2 managed to steady against the dollar yesterday and has pushed  \par \par \uc2 lower towards C$1.3190-C$1.3200 support this morning. The pair  \par \par \uc2 has broadly moved sideways in the past few days in what appears  \par \par \uc2 to be a pretty typical U.S. dollar bearish consolidation. This  \par \par \uc2 suggests some potential for the Canadian dollar to do better on  \par \par \uc2 a break under near-term support, which would then target a  \par \par \uc2 retest of C$1.3070-C$1.3080. But high anxiety in other markets  \par \par \uc2 may keep the Canadian dollar in a range for now. Resistance  \par \par \uc2 seen at C$1.3300-C$1.3325."  \par \par \uc2 KRISTIAN KERR, TECHNICAL ANALYST, \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  CAPITAL MARKETS:  \par \par \uc2 - EURO/DOLLAR: "Yesterday's breach of the 100-day simple  \par \par \uc2 moving average (SMA) in euro/dollar confirms Tuesday's failure  \par \par \uc2 at the 50-day exponential moving average (EMA); opening the way  \par \par \uc2 for a downside re-test of last week's $1.2056 low. Initial  \par \par \uc2 support is expected in the $1.2150 Fibonnaci zone, but as this  \par \par \uc2 level has already been penetrated once before, it loses some  \par \par \uc2 validity. In our view, the reaction at the weekly low will be  \par \par \uc2 pivotal in determining the pair's intermediate-term prospects.  \par \par \uc2 A close below sets up a more sinister correction to the 200-day  \par \par \uc2 SMA/double top measured objective, while a failure to penetrate  \par \par \uc2 gives rise to a potential bottoming process. The pair is  \par \par \uc2 nearing oversold on most daily oscillators but only a clear  \par \par \uc2 break back above the 50-day EMA undoes the damage done over the  \par \par \uc2 last two days."  \par \par \uc2 - DOLLAR/YEN: "A more subdued day of trading in dollar/yen  \par \par \uc2 after Tuesday's wild swings in both directions. The close below  \par \par \uc2 the 111.00 handle/100-day SMA hints at a potential turn, but as  \par \par \uc2 the current consolidation looks eerily like a bull flag, we  \par \par \uc2 prefer to stand clear of the short-side until the short-term  \par \par \uc2 parabolic trend clearly breaks. Tuesday's intraday low marks  \par \par \uc2 the key level to watch, as a clear break should set up more  \par \par \uc2 meaningful downside. On the upside, only a close back above the  \par \par \uc2 200-day SMA negates the bearish implications of Monday's dark  \par \par \uc2 cloud cover pattern."  \par \par \uc2 - STERLING/CABLE: "More heavy follow-through selling in  \par \par \uc2 cable yesterday as the pair broke key Fibonnaci, trendline and  \par \par \uc2 weekly support at $1.8150. The expansion range down bar puts  \par \par \uc2 into play the $1.7800 100-day SMA/38.2 percent Fibonnaci  \par \par \uc2 retracement (of the move from $1.5600). A break there could  \par \par \uc2 turn things really ugly as the 200-day SMA and head & shoulders  \par \par \uc2 measured objective become potential targets. The pair is  \par \par \uc2 looking a bit overdone from an oscillator standpoint, but until  \par \par \uc2 the pair clearly fails to breach a meaningful support or the  \par \par \uc2 $1.8150 area is re-taken we prefer stay away from the long  \par \par \uc2 side."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 12:10 p.m. EST (17:10 GMT). All data  \par \par \uc2 taken from Reuters calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m.  \par \par \uc2 (21:30 GMT) in the previous New York session.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Last    US Close  %      YTD     2003\par                               10 March  Change %Change Close\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.2262   1.2240   +0.18   -2.51   1.2578\par Dlr/yen              110.96   110.77   +0.17   +3.40   107.31\par Euro/yen             136.08   135.49   +0.44   +