\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar extends gains on profit-taking in euro.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Parry  \par \uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 17:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 10 (Reuters) - The dollar rose 1 percent against the euro on Wednesday as traders shrugged off news of a wider-than-expected U.S. January trade deficit and instead sold the euro, taking profits on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent gains.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said that profit-taking in euros and technically driven trading, not economic data, were boosting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Within the more long-term cycle in the dollar bear market, we are seeing a counter-trend rally in the dollar. Sometimes, during these periods, the underlying fundamentals move to the background," said Paresh Upadhyaya, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with Putnam Investments in Boston.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said they were wary of buying the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it slipped below a key technical area against the dollar between $1.2330 and $1.2350 in the prior session.  \par \par \uc2 That paved the way for the euro's fall on Wednesday, and the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also crashed below support against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "Basically, it's Japanese stop-loss selling of euro/yen below 135.85 yen. That was the key support," said Phillip Capone, vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives at Fortis Bank.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By late morning in New York, the euro was down more than 1 percent\par against the yen  at 135.63 yen. Against the dollar, the euro        was\par down 1.0 percent around $1.2196.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro has shed about seven cents since hitting record highs against the dollar above $1.2900 in mid-February.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Against the yen , the dollar was down about 0.3 percent to 110.90 yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Against the Swiss franc , the dollar was up about 0.7 percent to 1.2905 francs.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sterling was down about 1.5 percent to $1.7986.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. January trade deficit came in at $43.06 billion, compared with a revised December deficit of $42.69 billion. Economists' median forecasts had been for a January trade deficit of $42.05 billion.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After a brief bounce higher, the euro fell back into a deepening retreat against the dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't think (the report) changes the big picture," said Sean Callow, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with IDEAglobal in New York. "Those who are bearish on the dollar over the course of the year will have their expectations reinforced. They will see this in line with that bearish view, that the dollar still has further to fall to help correct the (U.S. trade) deficit."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Europe, European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governing Council member Ernst Welteke said the German economy was showing signs of recovering, but only at a very sluggish pace. He said the country's economic trend depended more on global growth than exchange rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors remained on alert for yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese monetary authorities, although upward pressure on the yen was alleviated by an unexpected downward revision in Japan's growth data for October-December.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan said the economy grew 1.6 percent in the October-December period from the previous quarter, revising down its initial reading of 1.7 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday after the dollar tumbled toward 110 yen. Money market analysts in Tokyo estimated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  probably \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to the tune of 500 billion yen ($4.50 billion). There was no confirmation from the authorities.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Daniel Bases, Gertrude Chavez and Manuela Badawy in New York and Natsuko Waki in London).   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040310e03a002yi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
