\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Retreats But Data, MOF Support Vs Yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 792 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar extended its retreat against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia Tuesday, but disappointing Japanese data and suspected bids by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported the greenback against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 The euro climbed roughly half a cent from its late New York level, while sterling rose nearly a cent. Both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit their highest levels since early last week.  \par \par \uc2 But the dollar held steady against the yen, thanks largely to bids that traders said originated from agent banks of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on behalf of the MOF. A brief pause in official bidding Monday precipitated a one-yen plunge in the dollar overnight.  \par \par \uc2 "The MOF needed to take some of the air out" of the dollar's rally, the head dealer at a European brokerage in Tokyo said of Monday's evaporation of the ministry's bids above Y112. He said a recent rise in speculative bets on the yen had put the dollar in danger of an even sharper short-covering fall had Tokyo not applied the brakes.  \par \par \uc2 "But if they don't support the dollar here and now," he said, "I think it could quickly fall below Y109."  \par \par \uc2 He cited "an even bigger" glut of stop-loss sell orders below Y111.00 than that which fueled the dollar's slide Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Later Tuesday, official support for the dollar was bolstered by much worse than expected Japanese machinery orders data.  \par \par \uc2 Core orders slumped 12.2% in January from a month earlier, the government said, suggesting recent strong corporate capital spending may slow. Economists surveyed by Dow Jones and Nikkei News had predicted a 0.4% decline.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y111.18, just above Y111.16 late Monday in New York but well below Y112.13 late Monday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.244, slightly off its intraday high around 1.2454 but above $1.2404 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $1.2370 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y138.36, up from Y137.83 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y138.72 in Tokyo late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8562, up from $1.8490 in New York and higher than $1.8466 in Tokyo Monday. Sterling climbed as high of 1.8582. [ 09-03-04 0537GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  data suggested Tokyo may not have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  as heavily as many thought to drive the yen to a five-month high Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Commercial banks' account balances at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose by Y1.2 trillion Tuesday, pointing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $10 billion or less. Traders had estimated the BOJ spent as much as $20 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Still, some traders and analysts said comments by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow Monday may signal that U.S. patience is growing thin with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Snow repeated the U.S. preference for a strong dollar but added that "no \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be considered strong if it is propped up on life support with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The remark followed Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's unusually blunt warning last week that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's "awesome" accumulation of dollar reserves via \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "will have to slow at some point and eventually cease."  \par \par \uc2 "It's a wonder that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been able to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as heavily as it has without provoking U.S. criticism," said Satoshi Tate, a vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank. "The U.S. isn't that generous."  \par \par \uc2 Tate predicted the dollar would stick to a broad range between Y110 and Y112 in the next few weeks.  \par \par \uc2 But others said the bulk of risks for the dollar/yen lie to the downside.  \par \par \uc2 A measure of trade flows by J.P. Morgan suggests short positions against the yen stand at their highest levels since last June, said Tohru Sasaki, a strategist for the bank in Tokyo. That augurs for a position-driven reversal, he said.  \par \par \uc2 The yen is trading close to its weakest levels in the past ten years in trade-weighted terms, Sasaki added.  \par \par \uc2 "Fundamentals and positioning are clearly positive for the yen," he said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f2