\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Mizoguchi: Sharp Short-Term  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Moves Unwarranted  \b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 01:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A top Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates tend to be volatile in the short-term, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gyrations ought to reflect economic fundamentals and shouldn't be too excessive.  \par \par \uc2 "It is desirable that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should move stably in the mid-term," Vice-Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi told reporters. [ 09-03-04 0057GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 "There is short-term volatility in the market, but it shouldn't be too sharp," Mizoguchi said.  \par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he also said the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance is unchanged, suggesting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 As of 0056 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y111.30, up slightly after a rapid drop overnight in New York to Y111.15 from the Y112 level.  \par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Gibson [ 09-03-04 0108GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040309e0390000o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
