\par\par \b \uc2 Tanigaki:  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Mkt Correcting From Post-Dubai Speculation  \b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 00:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister said Tuesday the dollar is still correcting from weakness driven by speculation, suggesting he believes a further rise in the greenback against the yen is justified.  \par \par \uc2 "It appears (the dollar) is currently in the process of correcting rapid movements which occurred due to a misunderstanding of the Dubai (Group of Seven) statement," Sadakazu Tanigaki told a regular news conference.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar weakened in the wake of the G7 finance officials meeting in Dubai last September amid speculation the G7 would tolerate a decline in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a means of adjusting the U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials have claimed this view was a misunderstanding and have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to reverse the dollar's decline. [ 09-03-04 0004GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , acting through the Bank of Japan, has spent more than Y10 trillion so far this year \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, even as the dollar continues to rebound sharply off a three-year low of Y105.16 marked in mid-February. At 0037 GMT Tuesday, the dollar was trading at Y111.36.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo officials claim their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at curbing speculative \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements which don't reflect economic fundamentals. Tanigaki also repeated Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not aimed at guiding \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates to specific levels.  \par \par \uc2 Recent comments by Tanigaki and other Japanese officials suggest that despite the market's growing alarm at the MOF's unabashed drive to boost the dollar and drive down the yen, the government feels justified in continuing to reverse what it sees as a tide of speculative dollar weakness seen since Dubai.  \par \par \uc2 Some in the market believe the MOF may be aiming to bring the dollar back up to levels near Y115 where it was trading before the September G7 meeting.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki declined to elaborate, however, on specific \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics. "There are times when (market) speculation regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is correct, but there are times when such speculation is wrong. We don't comment on that."  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki also said he would refrain from commenting on overnight remarks from U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow that suggested the U.S. finance chief disapproved of heavy-handed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But Tanigaki added that, from what he has read in the media reports, Snow must have commented "after considering a lot of things."  \par \par \uc2 Snow said Monday "we favor a strong dollar, but the relative value of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are best set through open and competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets." He added, "no \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be considered strong if it is propped up on life support with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale [ 09-03-04 0042GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040308e038000y9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\