\par\par \b \uc2 BoJ Fukui: Some Distance Before Getting Out Of Deflation  \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 09:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BASEL (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head said the country had some way to go before it would emerge from the price deflation that has resulted from a decade-long economic slump.  \par \par \uc2 Asked whether consumer prices in Japan would soon rise, Toshihiko Fukui, governor of the Bank of Japan, said: "We have some distance to go before we are out of deflation."  \par \par \uc2 He declined to discuss the current value of the yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 Traders say Japanese authorities have been conducting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at unprecedentedly high volumes to weaken the yen ahead of the end of the fiscal year March 31.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is believed to have sold yen to buy as much as $20 billion Friday alone. The move drove the dollar over a yen to Y112.27, a four-month high.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at Y112.17 early in Europe Monday, having reached a fresh high of Y112.28 overnight in Asian dealings.  \par \par \uc2 -By Adam Cohen, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 7776 200 923; adam.cohen@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (Adriana Arai in London contributed to this story.) [ 08-03-04 0917GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040308e038000bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
