\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Up Vs Yen As Japan MOF Keeps Up Pressure  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 758 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar rose slightly against the yen in Asia Monday, as jitters over Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities' aggressive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last week kept dollar bears at bay.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders had expected the dollar to turn down sharply against the yen in Tokyo trading hours, since its surge to a five-month high in New York Friday was fast pitched and bucked the greenback's broad downtrend against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. unit stayed comfortably above Y112, as few players were willing to go short dollar/yen amid the looming shadow of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan, which acts on behalf of the MOF, was estimated by some to have bought a hefty $20 billion in New York Friday an effort that eventually sent the greenback up over a yen to levels above Y112.  \par \par \uc2 Some warned the MOF remained active in the Tokyo market. A U.S. bank dealer said he spotted Japanese banks often associated with official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  placing bids around Y112.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF "is likely in the market...there are buyback orders of yen longs below Y112," so Japan's authorities look determined to defend that level, he said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro briefly fell below $1.2340 but rebounded on bids by non-Japanese players covering short euro positions, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "Some players unwound their positions after going short euro/dollar on the hope that Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities will conduct more aggressive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and spark a broad-based dollar rally," a European bank dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Many traders expect the euro to trade in a range of $1.2200-$1.2600 this week.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y112.13, above Y112.04 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at Y111.31 late Friday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2370, up from $1.2364 late Friday in New York. The euro was at $1.2207 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y138.72, up from Y138.57 in New York late Friday. The euro was at Y135.89 in Tokyo late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8466, up from $1.8456 in New York and higher than $1.8220 in Tokyo Friday. [ 08-03-04 0538GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Now that the MOF has shown its resolve to step into the market even after the dollar has surged well above Y105, which was previously considered its "line-in-the-sand," market players are pondering how far the ministry will go in its aggressive yen-selling campaign.  \par \par \uc2 Some players speculate that the MOF wants the dollar to rise to around Y115, a level that Tokyo surrendered half a year ago on heavy yen buying, sparked by the Group of Seven nations' call for more flexibility in exchange rates at their meeting in Dubai.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF may be particularly tempted to push up the dollar to around that level ahead of the March 31 fiscal year end so that Japanese exporters and other companies that need to repatriate yen can do so at more favorable rates.  \par \par \uc2 Tomoko Fujii, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Nikko Citigroup, said that from a technical view point, there was a good chance for the dollar to climb as high as Y115.50 by March 31.  \par \par \uc2 But she expressed doubts about the sustainability of the dollar's uptrend against the yen, warning that the ministry "is unlikely to keep selling yen aggressively above Y110" beyond the March 31 book-closing period.  \par \par \uc2 Traders also warned that further MOF action won't be justified amid growing signs that Japan's economy is on track for a full-fledged recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone can be described as market manipulation and will surely irritate European nations," an analyst at a Japanese brokerage house said. "Any remarks from the U.S. and Europe criticizing \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may shift the market trend in favor of the yen again," he said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 08-03-04 0652GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040308e0380004y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
